     xmlns:owl="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#"
     xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#"
     xmlns:xml="http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace"
     xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#"
     xmlns:rdfs="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#"
     xmlns:skos="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#"
     xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/">
    <owl:Ontology rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/holly2012/ontologies/2016/SGA_Pattern">
        <dcterms:description rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Diagram (this article has no graphical representation) | Intent: | Link to OWL File: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/HollyFerguson/Spatial-Graph-Adapter-Pattern/master/SGA\Protege\OWL.owlPDF of SGA Pattern Image: Image:USOcore3.pdfTo answer the modern, interdisciplinary questions asked within the Building domain, industry tools and data standards need to become f...</dcterms:description>
        <dcterms:title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Spatial Graph Adapter (SGA) Pattern</dcterms:title>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Curated by OntoBoard 1.155.0, so that the pattern passes ODK&apos;s quality report with its default profile, names every term with a label, and is consistent and coherent. Changes: label added x14; term declared x2;
- header: dcterms:title &quot;Spatial Graph Adapter (SGA) Pattern&quot; - the library&apos;s name for the pattern
- header: dcterms:description - the library&apos;s description of the pattern
- axiom removed: ObjectPropertyDomain(&lt;http://www.semanticweb.org/holly2012/ontologies/2016/SGA_Pattern#hasType&gt; &lt;http://www.semanticweb.org/holly2012/ontologies/2016/SGA_Pattern#Attribute&gt;) - two rdfs:domain axioms mean their intersection, and the pattern makes Attribute and ContextualizedRelation disjoint while each has exactly one hasType - so both were unsatisfiable; the domain is their union, the one reading under which both classes&apos; own restrictions hold
- axiom added: ObjectPropertyDomain(&lt;http://www.semanticweb.org/holly2012/ontologies/2016/SGA_Pattern#hasType&gt; ObjectUnionOf(&lt;http://www.semanticweb.org/holly2012/ontologies/2016/SGA_Pattern#Attribute&gt; &lt;http://www.semanticweb.org/holly2012/ontologies/2016/SGA_Pattern#ContextualizedRelation&gt;)) - two rdfs:domain axioms mean their intersection, and the pattern makes Attribute and ContextualizedRelation disjoint while each has exactly one hasType - so both were unsatisfiable; the domain is their union, the one reading under which both classes&apos; own restrictions hold
- axiom removed: ObjectPropertyDomain(&lt;http://www.semanticweb.org/holly2012/ontologies/2016/SGA_Pattern#hasType&gt; &lt;http://www.semanticweb.org/holly2012/ontologies/2016/SGA_Pattern#ContextualizedRelation&gt;) - replaced by the union above
Each change is listed under &quot;curated&quot; in the pattern&apos;s metadata.json in OntoBoard&apos;s pattern library.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Ontology>
    


